WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.324
The takeaway is that you can unfold detector
effects directly at the level of moments,

00:00:05.404 --> 00:00:07.209
without ever binning the data.

00:00:07.289 --> 00:00:12.614
Moment Unfolding does this with a GAN-like
generator whose parameters are the moments,

00:00:12.694 --> 00:00:15.064
trains only once rather than iterating,

00:00:15.144 --> 00:00:21.537
and recovers the true moments to better than a
hundredth of a percent on realistic LHC jet simulations.

00:00:21.617 --> 00:00:24.616
Because the algorithm is agnostic to the dataset,

00:00:24.696 --> 00:00:30.020
the same idea could carry over to deconvolution
problems well beyond particle physics.
